<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{180}(A)=J\cdot A\cdot J," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>180</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{180}(A)=J\cdot A\cdot J,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p2.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math> is the exchange matrix. Finally, for each subregion, we have</p>
<table id="S3.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
